  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Thai Chicken Satay",
  "text": "Thai Chicken Satay\n\nPreparation time: 15 minutes plus 2 hours marrinade\n\nCooking time: 8 minutes\n\nYield:\n\nIngredients\n\n500g chicken breast ( cut into 1 in wide 3 in long)\n\n8-10 bamboo skewers.\n\nFor the marinade\n\n1/2 cup coconut milk,\n\n2 tbsp minced galangal,\n\n2 tbsp minced lemon grass,\n\n1 tbsp coriander powder,\n\n1-2 tbsp turmeric or curry powder,\n\n1 tsp salt,\n\n1-2 tsp sugar,\n\n1-2 tsp white or black pepper.\n\nFor the satay sauce\n\n1/2- 3/4 cup coconut milk\n\n1/4 cup coarsely ground roast peanut or peanut\n\n1/4 cup red curry paste\n\n1/4 cup tamarind juice\n\n1 tsp salt or fish sauce\n\nFor the cucumber relish sauce\n\n2 red spur chillies ( finely sliced)\n\n1 cucumber ( sliced in quarters lenght then sliced thin)\n\n1-2 shallot ( finely chopped)\n\n1/2 sugar\n\n1/2 cup vinegar\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Cut the chicken into thin wide strips. A single strip will be threaded on a skewer lengthways.\n\n2. Make the marinade, by combining all the dry ingredients in a food processor, then adding the liquids.\n\n3. Add the chicken to the marinade, cover with clingfilm, and refrigerate for 2 hours.\n\n4. To make the satay sauce, put the coarsely ground peanuts in a pan,then add the red curry paste, and coconut milk. Bring to the boil, then turn down the heat and add the remaining ingredients.\n\n5. To make the cucumber relish, put the vinegar in a small pan, add the sugar, and dissolve over  low heat. Turn off the heat and allow to cool. Add the cucumber, shallot and chilli.",
  "cookTime": "PT8M",
